			],
			"Message": "refactor(Wind): Strip Effect monad from Editor and TextModelResolver services\n\nContinue the de-Effectification of low-level Wind service bindings, following the pattern established in the Commands service (f97e5dd). Both EditorService and TextModelResolverService convert their Effect.Effect return types to native sync/Promise signatures.\n\nEditorService:\n- Sync getters (GetActiveEditor, GetVisibleEditors, GetSelections) return plain values instead of Effect<..., EditorProblem>.\n- Async methods (OpenEditor, CloseEditor, etc.) return Promise<T> instead of Effect<T, EditorProblem>.\n- Delete the EditorServiceTag reference and Layer.succeed wrapper from Live.ts. Export LiveEditorServiceLayer as the plain service object.\n- Replace the tagged union EditorProblem type with plain Error via MakeEditorProblem.\n\nTextModelResolverService:\n- Interface methods (Resolve, HasModel, Reload) return Promise<T> instead of Effect<T, TextModelResolverProblem>.\n- Delete TextModelResolverServiceTag and Layer.succeed wrapper from Live.ts. Export LiveTextModelResolverServiceLayer as the plain service object.\n- Bridge the ModelService (which still uses Effect) via Effect.runPromise wrappers (OpenModel, GetModel, CloseModel) at the top of the module, isolating Effect imports to a single bridge boundary.\n- Replace MakeResolverProblem tagged union with plain Error.\n\nThis reduces runtime overhead from Effect pipeline construction for these thin Tauri IPC wrappers where no composition, retry, or scheduling guarantees are required.",
			"SHA": "ae827284cc4b3c44f88e7069e3b369a5092b1afc"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T21:56:18Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				906,
				2
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Wind): Strip Effect monad from Commands service\n\nRemove the Effect.Effect return types from the CommandsService interface and\nthe corresponding Effect pipeline wrappers in the Live implementation.\nRegisterCommand and UnregisterCommand become void-returning sync calls;\nExecuteCommand and GetCommands return native Promise<T> instead of\nEffect<T, CommandsProblem>.\n\nDelete the CommandsServiceTag, LiveCommandsServiceLayer, and\nCommandsOperationFailed error type. Replace MakeCommandsOperationFailed\nwith a plain MakeCommandsError helper. The module now exports\nCommandsServiceInstance directly.\n\nThis aligns with the ongoing de-Effectification of low-level Wind service\nbindings that delegate directly to Tauri IPC — async/await is sufficient\nwhere no composition or retry/scheduling guarantees are required.",
			"SHA": "f97e5ddf7eb74491ef8992e16ab70c1d16ab2e03"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T21:54:27Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				906,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Wind): Replace runtime process.env TierShim with compile-time esbuild define\n\nSubstitute the runtime `process.env[\"TierShim\"]` lookup at module load with a `declare const __LandTier_Shim__` that esbuild replaces at build time via its `define` substitution mechanism. The previous approach prevented esbuild from dead-code-eliminating the Shim module when TierShim=None, since `process.env` is a dynamic reference the bundler cannot statically evaluate.\n\nAdd the `declare const` block following the established pattern in Cocoon's Main.ts, and document the full propagation chain: `.env.Land → TierEnvironment.sh → CocoonEsbuildDefine → esbuild config → __LandTier_Shim__ → this module`.\n\nThis enables esbuild to tree-shake the entire Shim subsystem (Type, Gate, SwallowMap, RedirectBus, IPCInterceptor, AuditLog) when TierShim is None, producing a smaller bundle with no behavioral change at runtime.",
			"SHA": "a91438b84876ddfcdd79078b588a46efe445be48"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T21:50:45Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				906,
				9
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Wind): Prune orphaned ActivityBar module files\n\nFollowing the barrel-export cleanup in 339051da, delete the remaining 9 ActivityBar source files that were left on disk. The Shim system's SwallowMap now routes ActivityBar IPC calls at the proxy layer, rendering this Effect-based service module unreachable.\n\nRemove the full Source/Effect/ActivityBar/ subtree: types, errors, implementation, helpers, mock layer, and barrel index. No imports reference these files from any remaining Wind source.",
			"SHA": "fc419e316de17b25c7c674c41ca7a55d60667653"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T21:50:18Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				921,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Wind): Remove defunct ActivityBar Effect module and barrel exports\n\nThe ActivityBar Effect service module — types, errors, implementations, and mock — was built for direct VS Code workbench integration that Land no longer uses. The Shim system's SwallowMap now routes ActivityBar IPC calls at the proxy layer, and the WorkbenchLayout bridge references \"ActivityBar\" only as a layout-section string constant, not the deleted service.\n\nDelete the entire `Source/Effect/ActivityBar/` subtree (9 files) and strip the corresponding type, implementation, and error exports from the Effect barrel (`Source/Effect/index.ts`). This eliminates 13 lines of stale re-exports that would block tree-shaking and confuse consumers.\n\nNo callers remain — confirmed by content search across the Wind source tree.",
			"SHA": "339051dadd7191f894987c4f464182fdca241302"
		}
	],
